{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388751-what-are-lore-excellencies-good-for-which-ones-are-best-2nd-ed","id":1388751,"title":"What are Lore Excellencies good for? Which ones are best? (2nd Ed.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-15T13:50:04-07:00","id":1388751,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What are Lore Excellencies good for? Which ones are best? (2nd Ed.)","content":"A lot of good Lore Charms in <b>2nd Edition</b> have 2 Lore Excellencies as their requirement, but I'm not sure there are that many Lore rolls that could benefit from an Excellency. Is it just a double speed bump because the Charms behind them are that good, or is there a use of them I am ignorant of?<br /> <br /> Also, which Lore Excellencies would you pick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 05-16-2020, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T16:53:56-07:00","id":1388791,"title":"","content":"It's been a long time, but I remember my preference being for 2nd and 3rd.<br /> <br /> Lore rolls rarely have such high difficulties that the potential big rolls of the 1st mattered nearly as much as the sure successes of the 2nd, and the 3rd was in case you flubbed an easy roll that shouldn't have needed a Charm 95% or more of the time.<br /> <br /> Though someone else might have some specific reason for a different selection I'm forgetting about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T19:13:02-07:00","id":1397874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388751-what-are-lore-excellencies-good-for-which-ones-are-best-2nd-ed?p=1388791#post1388791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long time, but I remember my preference being for 2nd and 3rd.<br /> <br /> Lore rolls rarely have such high difficulties that the potential big rolls of the 1st mattered nearly as much as the sure successes of the 2nd, and the 3rd was in case you flubbed an easy roll that shouldn't have needed a Charm 95% or more of the time.<br /> <br /> Though someone else might have some specific reason for a different selection I'm forgetting about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree, except since you don't tend to make tons of Lore rolls and they don't tend to be time sensitive, I'd say just take 2nd and pay the 2m any time you're worried. Heck, if you stunt it you get them right back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T21:36:18-07:00","id":1397892,"title":"","content":"The issue is, as noted by the OP, that the 2e Lore trees require two Excellencies as prerequisites for some main Charms (ex: Wyld Shaping Technique).<br /> <br /> 2nd Excellency is certainly the best for 2e Lore, but if you need two 3rd is the most logical second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T22:13:55-07:00","id":1397897,"title":"","content":"I don't recall any really great reason to go with both 1st and 2nd excellencies for any ability, and Lore is no exception. I also agree that 2nd makes more sense than 1st since lore rolls are less likely to be &quot;swingy&quot; - you're likely to get as much as you need out of the average lore check if you get 2 successes or 5. So, yeah, 2nd and 3rd would be my recommendation as well.<br /> <br /> That said, I've always found the double excellency requirement an unnecessary speedbump. I'd recommend talking to your ST about dropping it to one - or, if you're doing 2.5, considering how many other Solar trees drop Excellencies as requirements, possibly dropping them both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:54:16-07:00","id":1397936,"title":"","content":"3rd is best, then 2nd, in that order.<br /> <br /> Oh, we're talking about Excellencies?<br /> <br /> The real value of Essence Ressurgent is ease of bumping Static Values, which doesn't really apply to Lore. But realistically, if you are invested in Lore you are not going to be failing an average Lore roll. The Charms where you want to buy assurance with Essence Triumphant are gated behind two Excellencies anyway.<br /> <br /> Plus, unless your ST is a real stickler, they're not going to ask you to roll unless it's dramatically appropriate. At which point saying &quot;I spend 4m and auto succeed&quot; is a bit anti-climatic, whereas flubbing your &quot;sure-fire&quot; difficulty 2 roll on 10 dice gives you those &quot;Jehova starts with an &quot;i&quot;!&quot; moments.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I agree with the crowd, no reason to buy Essence Overwhelming for Lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}